Hi Avery,

GitHub Universe 2026 is October 28 and 29 at Fort Mason in San Francisco, and early-bird pricing ends this Friday, September 18.

Two days of:
- Keynotes on where Copilot, Actions, and the platform are going next
- 100+ sessions on developer productivity, security, and AI-assisted development
- Hands-on labs and certification exams
- The startup lounge, with office hours from GitHub's startup team

Early-bird in-person passes are $699 (regular $999). Virtual passes are free.

Register: https://explore.github.com/l/universe-2026?c=early

Not sure yet? Register for the virtual pass now and upgrade later.

See you in October,
